{"world_id":"wld_tidal_conservatories","characters":[{"id":"chr_nara_vel","name":"Nara Vel","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","faction_id":"fac_tide_wardens","description":"Nara Vel is a junior Tide Warden whose careful tide-table readings first reveal that the Glassgate sills are silting up weeks ahead of schedule. Raised among the Mangrove Terraces, she learned to read water by watching how silt gathered around the roots, then joined the Wardens to protect the whole lagoon rather than one garden. She is slight and quick-moving, with close-cropped dark hair, a weathered tide chart tucked into her coat, and fingertips stained by silt from repeated measurements. Nara is precise and patient in her work, but has little experience persuading people whose livelihoods depend on ignoring inconvenient evidence.","motivation":"Keep the lagoon's tide flowing through the gates so the city can continue to power its mills and feed its terraces.","goal":"Convince the guilds to pause the glassblowing season long enough for the Wardens to dredge the locks before the spring tide.","flaw":"She treats correct measurements as if they should be enough to win agreement, and withdraws when people challenge her authority.","internal_conflict":"Nara fears that, as a junior warden, she has mistaken an unusual reading for a crisis and will harm workers' livelihoods by insisting on a halt.","external_conflict":"The Glassblower Guild's firing calendar leaves little time to close the gates for dredging, while the accelerated silting threatens to restrict the tide that powers the city.","arc":"Nara begins by presenting her measurements as a report and retreating when the guild questions them. When a channel bell is found out of tune during the dispute, she chooses to bring the silt evidence and the bell's urgent recasting need together at Bellmaker's Quay, asking the Ferry Cooperative and guild to help verify the danger rather than demanding belief. By the end, she still values exact readings but can make a shared case for action, accepting responsibility for the consequences of a temporary kiln pause.","personality_traits":["observant","methodical","self-doubting","persistent"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tide-table reading","description":"Compares tide cycles and gate measurements to spot deviations in the lagoon's flow.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Silt assessment","description":"Identifies changes in silt depth and texture that can signal a blockage forming at the locks.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_orsen_kel","name":"Orsen Kel","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","faction_id":"fac_glassblower_guild","description":"Orsen Kel is a senior glassblower and the guild's keeper of the firing calendar, responsible for coordinating work at Bellmaker's Quay. He apprenticed there after his family lost its terrace plot in a lean season, and sees a full firing season as a promise of steady work for the guild's apprentices. Broad-shouldered and silver-haired, Orsen wears a heat-darkened apron and carries a small tuning fork used to check the channel bells. He is a skilled craftsperson and a forceful negotiator, but his pride in the guild's charter makes him reluctant to admit that its schedule can put the city at risk.","motivation":"Protect the craft and the livelihoods of the glassblowers who depend on the season's work.","goal":"Complete the planned firing season without losing the guild's authority over its bells and windows.","flaw":"He mistakes a concession on timing for surrendering the guild's standing and tends to dismiss warnings from junior wardens.","internal_conflict":"Orsen wants the guild to be trusted as a steward of the city, yet fears that pausing work will expose how much its charter depends on the tide.","external_conflict":"The Wardens need the gates shut for dredging before spring tide, while the guild's planned firing season depends on keeping the lagoon's flow available.","arc":"Orsen begins by refusing to shorten the firing season, convinced that a pause would weaken the guild. When Nara's measurements and a mistuned channel bell make the risks tangible at Bellmaker's Quay, he chooses to pause one firing cycle and have the guild recast the bell within the charter's day. He ends willing to treat the kiln calendar as a tool for the city's needs, not a claim that outranks them.","personality_traits":["proud","craft-minded","protective","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Bell tuning","description":"Recognizes when a channel bell's tone is wrong and can direct its recasting.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Guild negotiation","description":"Builds consensus among artisans by understanding their craft obligations and concerns.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tavi_ro","name":"Tavi Ro","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_algae_fields","faction_id":"fac_ferry_cooperative","description":"Tavi Ro is a ferry cooperative pilot who carries harvest, glass and dredged silt across the lagoon by sail and paddle. Their parents tended the Mangrove Terraces, and Tavi learned early that the silt from a cleared lock can enrich a garden only if someone hauls and spreads it within the season. Lean and sun-browned, they keep their hair under a reed cap and wear a ferry rope bracelet knotted with marks for each completed crossing. Tavi is practical, resourceful and quick to spot a workable route, but the cooperative's claim to dredged silt makes them defensive whenever the Wardens talk about the terraces as a commons.","motivation":"Ensure ferry crews are treated fairly for the dangerous, essential work of moving dredged silt.","goal":"Secure a clear agreement that assigns the dredged silt and its transport work before the cooperative commits its barges.","flaw":"They reduce disputes to questions of ownership and compensation, even when delay threatens everyone.","internal_conflict":"Tavi believes the cooperative deserves the value it hauls, but also remembers how terrace families depend on fertile silt and worries that insisting on a claim will repeat old scarcity.","external_conflict":"The Tide Wardens need the Ferry Cooperative's barges to move lock silt, while the cooperative and Wardens disagree over whether the silt belongs to the crews or the terrace commons.","arc":"Tavi begins by withholding barges until the silt-rights dispute is settled in the cooperative's favor. When the gates' silting threatens the tide and Nara shows how the lock oath and silt-debt rule apply, Tavi chooses to haul the first dredged load and record both the crew's labor and its delivery to the terraces. They end the story ready to negotiate fair credit without making ownership a reason to leave the locks blocked.","personality_traits":["practical","wary","resourceful","fair-minded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Lagoon navigation","description":"Pilots sail and paddle barges through the lagoon's channels using local water knowledge.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Cargo planning","description":"Organizes loads and crossings to move harvest, glass and silt efficiently.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_ina_sorel","name":"Ina Sorel","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","faction_id":"fac_tide_wardens","description":"Ina Sorel is a veteran Tide Warden who grew up tending the Mangrove Terraces and remembers the hunger that followed the Great Silting. She now helps gate crews prepare for spring tides, bringing a terrace grower's knowledge of roots and silt to the Wardens' engineering work. Compact and strong, with a streak of white through her braided hair, Ina wears a waterproof shoulder cape patched with small pieces of vitrified glass. She is calm under pressure and generous with younger workers, but her memory of past failure makes her overprotective and inclined to take every dangerous task onto herself.","motivation":"Prevent another season of hunger by keeping the locks clear and the terrace gardens supplied.","goal":"Get the crews, barges and terraces coordinated so the gates can be dredged before the spring tide.","flaw":"She assumes that protecting people means carrying the hardest work alone and withholding uncertainty until she has a solution.","internal_conflict":"Ina wants Nara to become a confident warden, but fears that letting her lead a risky public effort will expose the city to another Great Silting.","external_conflict":"The kiln calendar and the silt-rights dispute delay the cooperation needed to clear the locks before the spring tide.","arc":"Ina begins by shielding Nara from guild negotiations and trying to coordinate the dredging herself. When the lock oath demands action before spring tide and Nara proposes bringing the factions together, Ina chooses to stand beside her rather than take over the meeting. She ends willing to share both the risk and her knowledge of the Great Silting, helping younger wardens lead without concealing the danger from them.","personality_traits":["steady","protective","experienced","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Gate-crew coordination","description":"Organizes crews to clear locks in time for a spring tide.","category":"social"},{"name":"Root-garden knowledge","description":"Understands how silt and water conditions affect the Mangrove Terraces.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nara_orsen","source_character_id":"chr_nara_vel","target_character_id":"chr_orsen_kel","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Nara's warning that the gates must be dredged directly challenges Orsen's firing calendar; their dispute forces each to weigh citywide needs against the livelihoods they are sworn to protect."},{"id":"rel_orsen_nara","source_character_id":"chr_orsen_kel","target_character_id":"chr_nara_vel","relationship_type":"skeptic","description":"Orsen doubts Nara's authority as a junior warden and initially treats her measurements as an obstacle to the guild's season, making her case harder to deliver."},{"id":"rel_ina_nara","source_character_id":"chr_ina_sorel","target_character_id":"chr_nara_vel","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Ina mentors Nara in gate work and the memory of the Great Silting, but must learn to support Nara's leadership instead of speaking for her."},{"id":"rel_tavi_nara","source_character_id":"chr_tavi_ro","target_character_id":"chr_nara_vel","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tavi can move the dredged silt Nara needs cleared from the locks, while their disagreement over who owns it puts pressure on their practical alliance."},{"id":"rel_orsen_tavi","source_character_id":"chr_orsen_kel","target_character_id":"chr_tavi_ro","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Orsen and Tavi depend on each other's work to move glass and supplies across the lagoon, but the kiln pause threatens the guild's shipments and complicates their cooperation."}]}
