en begins by refusing to shorten the firing season, convinced that a pause would weaken the guild. When Nara's measurements and a mistuned channel bell make the risks tangible at Bellmaker's Quay, he chooses to pause one firing cycle and have the guild recast the bell within the charter's day. He ends willing to treat the kiln calendar as a tool for the city's needs, not a claim that outranks them.","personality_traits":["proud","craft-minded","protective","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Bell tuning","description":"Recognizes when a channel bell's tone is wrong and can direct its recasting.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Guild negotiation","description":"Builds consensus among artisans by understanding their craft obligations and concerns.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tavi_ro","name":"Tavi Ro","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_algae_fields","faction_id":"fac_ferry_cooperative","description":"Tavi Ro is a ferry cooperative pilot who carries harvest, glass and dredged silt across the lagoon by sail and paddle. Their parents tended the Mangrove Terraces, and Tavi learned early that the silt from a cleared lock can enrich a garden only if someone hauls and spreads it within the season. Lean and sun-browned, they keep their hair under a reed cap and wear a ferry rope bracelet knotted with marks for each completed crossing. Tavi is practical, resourceful and quick to spot a workable route, but the cooperative's claim to dredged silt makes them defensive whenever the Wardens talk about the terraces as a commons.","motivation":"Ensure ferry crews are treated fairly for the dangerous, essential work of moving dredged silt.","goal":"Secure a clear agreement that assigns the dredged silt and its transport work before the cooperative commits its barges.","flaw":"They reduce disputes to questions of ownership and compensation, even when delay threatens everyone.","internal_conflict":"Tavi believes the cooperative deserves the value it hauls, but also remembers how terrace families depend on fertile silt and worries that insisting on a claim will repeat old scarcity.","external_conflict":"The Tide Wardens need the Ferry Cooperative's barges to move lock silt, while the cooperative and Wardens disagree over whether the silt belongs to the crews or the terrace commons.","arc":"Tavi begins by withholding barges until the silt-rights dispute is settled in the cooperative's favor. When the gates' silting threatens the tide and Nara shows how the lock oath and silt-debt rule apply, Tavi chooses to haul the first dredged load and record both the crew's labor and its delivery to the terraces. They end the story ready to negotiate fair credit without making ownership a reason to leave the locks blocked.","personality_traits":["practical","wary","resourceful","fair-minded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Lagoon navigation","description":"Pilots sail and paddle barges through the lagoon's channels using local water knowledge.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Cargo planning","description":"Organizes loads and crossings to move harvest, glass and silt efficiently.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_ina_sorel","name":"Ina Sorel","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","faction_id":"fac_tide_wardens","description":"Ina Sorel is a veteran Tide Warden who grew up tending the Mangrove Terraces and remembers the hunger that followed the Great Silting. She now helps gate crews prepare for spring tides, bringing a terrace grower's knowledge of roots and silt to the Wardens' engineering work. Compact and strong, with a streak of white through her braided hair, Ina wears a waterproof shoulder cape patched with small pieces of vitrified glass. She is calm under pressure and generous with younger workers, but her memory of past failure makes her overprotective and inclined to take every dangerous task onto herself.","motivation":"Prevent another season of hunger by keeping the locks clear and the terrace gardens supplied.","goal":"Get the crews, barges and terraces coordinated so the gates can be dredged before the spring tide.","flaw":"She assumes that protecting people means carrying the hardest work alone and withholding uncertainty until she has a solution.","internal_conflict":"Ina wants Nara to become a confident warden, but fears that letting her lead a risky public effort will expose the city to another Great Silting.","external_conflict":"The kiln calendar and the silt-rights dispute delay the cooperation needed to clear the locks before the spring tide.","arc":"Ina begins by shielding Nara from guild negotiations and trying to coordinate the dredging herself. When the lock oath demands action before spring tide and Nara proposes bringing the factions together, Ina chooses to stand beside her rather than take over the meeting. She ends willing to share both the risk and her knowledge of the Great Silting, helping younger wardens lead without concealing the danger from them.","personality_traits":["steady","protective","experienced","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Gate-crew coordination","description":"Organizes crews to clear locks in time for a spring tide.","category":"social"},{"name":"Root-garden knowledge","description":"Understands how silt and water conditions affect the Mangrove Terraces.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nara_orsen","source_character_id":"chr_nara_vel","target_character_id":"chr_orsen_kel","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Nara's warning that the gates must be dredged directly challenges Orsen's firing calendar; their dispute forces each to weigh citywide needs against the livelihoods they are sworn to protect."},{"id":"rel_orsen_nara","source_character_id":"chr_orsen_kel","target_character_id":"chr_nara_vel","relationship_type":"skeptic","description":"Orsen doubts Nara's authority as a junior warden and initially treats her measurements as an obstacle to the guild's season, making her case harder to deliver."},{"id":"rel_ina_nara","source_character_id":"chr_ina_sorel","target_character_id":"chr_nara_vel","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Ina mentors Nara in gate work and the memory of the Great Silting, but must learn to support Nara's leadership instead of speaking for her."},{"id":"rel_tavi_nara","source_character_id":"chr_tavi_ro","target_character_id":"chr_nara_vel","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tavi can move the dredged silt Nara needs cleared from the locks, while their disagreement over who owns it puts pressure on their practical alliance."},{"id":"rel_orsen_tavi","source_character_id":"chr_orsen_kel","target_character_id":"chr_tavi_ro","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Orsen and Tavi depend on each other's work to move glass and supplies across the lagoon, but the kiln pause threatens the guild's shipments and complicates their cooperation."}]}
