al":"Get the crews, barges and terraces coordinated so the gates can be dredged before the spring tide.","flaw":"She assumes that protecting people means carrying the hardest work alone and withholding uncertainty until she has a solution.","internal_conflict":"Ina wants Nara to become a confident warden, but fears that letting her lead a risky public effort will expose the city to another Great Silting.","external_conflict":"The kiln calendar and the silt-rights dispute delay the cooperation needed to clear the locks before the spring tide.","arc":"Ina begins by shielding Nara from guild negotiations and trying to coordinate the dredging herself. When the lock oath demands action before spring tide and Nara proposes bringing the factions together, Ina chooses to stand beside her rather than take over the meeting. She ends willing to share both the risk and her knowledge of the Great Silting, helping younger wardens lead without concealing the danger from them.","personality_traits":["steady","protective","experienced","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Gate-crew coordination","description":"Organizes crews to clear locks in time for a spring tide.","category":"social"},{"name":"Root-garden knowledge","description":"Understands how silt and water conditions affect the Mangrove Terraces.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nara_orsen","source_character_id":"chr_nara_vel","target_character_id":"chr_orsen_kel","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Nara's warning that the gates must be dredged directly challenges Orsen's firing calendar; their dispute forces each to weigh citywide needs against the livelihoods they are sworn to protect."},{"id":"rel_orsen_nara","source_character_id":"chr_orsen_kel","target_character_id":"chr_nara_vel","relationship_type":"skeptic","description":"Orsen doubts Nara's authority as a junior warden and initially treats her measurements as an obstacle to the guild's season, making her case harder to deliver."},{"id":"rel_i