{"world_id":"wld_crane_banner_coast","characters":[{"id":"chr_lin_suyin","name":"Lin Suyin","role":"protagonist","description":"A disowned sword-student from Thunder Reed Dojo, Suyin inherited her late master's weather-dark tally-stick and the duty of carrying it to the sects named upon it. She was cast out after refusing to repeat a challenge she believed had been falsified. Lean and long-limbed, she wears a patched reed-cloth coat and keeps her sword wrapped until a formal challenge is witnessed.","motivation":"Honor her master's final trust without letting the tally become an excuse for another feud.","goal":"Reach the three parties named on the tally and secure their envoys for a peace moot before the rookery's cranes are driven away.","flaw":"She treats self-reliance as proof of worth and hides uncertainty until others mistake it for defiance.","internal_conflict":"She fears that accepting her master's legacy means accepting the dojo's judgment that she is unfit to belong.","external_conflict":"The Crane Sect and Eel School dispute whether a disowned student's presentation of the tally binds them, while the nesting ban and fishing claims strain toward violence.","arc":"Suyin begins convinced that she must prove the tally's authority alone. When the Crane Sect demands that she submit it to Bannerhall's challenge records before it will witness her claim, she chooses to ask Salt Warden Mei for testimony rather than force the matter with her sword. By the moot's end, she accepts that carrying her master's trust means sharing its burden, not earning back a place by herself.","personality_traits":["observant","reserved","steadfast","wry"],"abilities":[{"name":"Reed-running","description":"Uses the light-body art to cross marsh reeds and dojo rooftops, but cannot use it over open water.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Measured blade","description":"A disciplined swordswoman who waits for a witnessed formal challenge rather than drawing first.","category":"physical"}],"home_location_id":"loc_thunder_reed_dojo"},{"id":"chr_qiao_ren","name":"Qiao Ren","role":"antagonist","description":"The Eel School's senior envoy, Qiao Ren grew up hearing that the Net Wars ended with his family's fishing rights left unresolved. Broad-shouldered and scarred by years hauling nets, he wears a dark eel-scale mantle and carries a plain practice sword. He is forceful in council, but insists that every blade be drawn only after Bannerhall witnesses a formal challenge.","motivation":"Keep his school from surrendering the fishing grounds his family believes were taken from them.","goal":"Win a lawful decision allowing the Eel School to fish the rookery shallows once nesting ends, and prevent the tally from deciding the question before debate.","flaw":"He mistakes compromise for a permanent loss and turns every concession into a test of strength.","internal_conflict":"He wants the Net Wars' scarcity never to return, yet fears that yielding even temporarily will leave his people hungry and forgotten.","external_conflict":"The Crane Sect enforces the nesting ban, while Suyin's tally may oblige the Eel School to send an envoy to a moot before its claim is settled.","arc":"Qiao Ren begins by treating Suyin's tally as a threat to his school's rights. At Bannerhall, when he can formally challenge her but sees that the cranes have begun abandoning the nesting islets, he chooses to send an envoy to the moot instead of demanding an immediate contest. He ends willing to argue for the Eel School's rights through the pact, rather than by forcing a decision at the rookery.","personality_traits":["forceful","proud","protective","pragmatic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Net-hook forms","description":"Uses a hooked practice blade and close footwork shaped by years working fishing nets.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Resource tally","description":"Keeps careful accounts of catches and provisions, giving him a sharp sense of how scarcity affects his school.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mist_rookery","faction_id":"fac_eel_school"},{"id":"chr_shen_yue","name":"Shen Yue","role":"supporting","description":"A Crane Sect covenant witness at Bannerhall, Shen Yue has spent years recording challenges beneath the pact's banners. Tall and fine-boned, she dresses in pale layered robes with ink stains at the cuffs and carries a narrow ledger case instead of a visible weapon. She believes rules matter most when they restrain the powerful as well as the desperate.","motivation":"Preserve the Crane Banner pact as a protection against another Broken Challenge.","goal":"Determine whether the tally-stick was properly presented and record any envoy commitment under the covenant.","flaw":"She trusts procedure so completely that she can mistake a fair process for a fair outcome.","internal_conflict":"She fears that bending the covenant for a worthy cause will weaken the only safeguard that kept sects from returning to the Net Wars.","external_conflict":"The Crane Sect's authority to witness challenges is questioned when Suyin, disowned by her school, invokes the tally's obligation.","arc":"Shen Yue begins by refusing to treat Suyin's word as sufficient evidence. When the tally's worn inscription matches the Crane Sect's old challenge record, she chooses to enter the presentation in the ledger despite pressure to dismiss it on Suyin's status alone. She ends prepared to uphold the pact's obligations even when its protections complicate her own sect's position.","personality_traits":["precise","patient","cautious","principled"],"abilities":[{"name":"Covenant memory","description":"Recalls the procedures and precedents governing formal challenges at Bannerhall.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Witness's voice","description":"Can keep a tense assembly focused on the recorded terms of a challenge.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_bannerhall","faction_id":"fac_crane_sect"},{"id":"chr_mei_tanshu","name":"Mei Tanshu","role":"supporting","description":"A senior Salt Warden on Saltmarket Isle, Mei Tanshu safeguards the market peace and the safe conduct of envoys. Compact and silver-haired, she wears a salt-blue sash and a weatherproof travel cloak, carrying a wooden staff marked with market tallies. She remembers the Broken Challenge as a warning that neutrality takes work, not distance.","motivation":"Keep Saltmarket Isle safe enough that rival sects can still meet and speak.","goal":"Get the named parties to accept safe conduct and attend the moot without turning the market into another battlefield.","flaw":"She withholds her own judgment for so long that others can mistake restraint for indifference.","internal_conflict":"She wants to remain neutral, but knows that refusing to speak when the peace is threatened can itself favor the stronger party.","external_conflict":"The disputed tally could draw sect envoys into the market, where the memory of the Broken Challenge makes every promise of safe conduct fragile.","arc":"Mei begins determined to offer only the neutral protections of the market peace. When Qiao Ren considers rejecting the tally and Suyin risks losing the chance to call a moot, Mei chooses to testify that she saw Suyin arrive carrying the master's stick under safe conduct. She ends still impartial between the fishing claims, but no longer silent about the conditions needed for a fair meeting.","personality_traits":["measured","diplomatic","watchful","resolute"],"abilities":[{"name":"Safe-conduct negotiation","description":"Secures practical terms for envoys to meet under the Salt Wardens' market peace.","category":"social"},{"name":"Harbor staff","description":"Uses a sturdy wooden staff for balance on slick docks and defense without drawing a sect's sword.","category":"physical"}],"home_location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","faction_id":"fac_salt_wardens"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_suyin_qiao","source_character_id":"chr_lin_suyin","target_character_id":"chr_qiao_ren","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Lin Suyin and Qiao Ren disagree over whether the tally should compel an envoy before the Eel School's fishing claim is heard."},{"id":"rel_qiao_shen","source_character_id":"chr_qiao_ren","target_character_id":"chr_shen_yue","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Qiao Ren sees Shen Yue's enforcement of the nesting ban as a threat to his school's livelihood; Shen Yue sees his pressure as a test of the covenant."},{"id":"rel_suyin_mei","source_character_id":"chr_lin_suyin","target_character_id":"chr_mei_tanshu","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mei Tanshu offers Suyin safe conduct and, when the tally is disputed, becomes a witness to her arrival at Saltmarket Isle."},{"id":"rel_suyin_shen","source_character_id":"chr_lin_suyin","target_character_id":"chr_shen_yue","relationship_type":"uneasy_ally","description":"Shen Yue doubts Suyin's authority at first, but their shared commitment to witnessed procedure brings them into a cautious alliance."},{"id":"rel_mei_qiao","source_character_id":"chr_mei_tanshu","target_character_id":"chr_qiao_ren","relationship_type":"mediator","description":"Mei Tanshu insists that Qiao Ren's claim be heard under market peace rather than settled through pressure on the rookery."}]}
