s as well as company claims, accepting that procedure only protects workers when it can expose its own gaps.","personality_traits":["steadfast","cautious","duty-bound","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Roster auditing","description":"Can reconcile duty logs, shift limits, and safety records to identify discrepancies.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Crew mediation","description":"Can negotiate practical agreements between riggers under pressure without ignoring the safety charter.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_sela_morin","name":"Sela Morin","role":"supporting","description":"Sela is a Charter Audit Office examiner stationed in the Bastion Hulk. She arrived after the Audit Charter established a permanent berth and built her reputation on catching discrepancies that others dismissed as clerical noise. Neat and spare in manner, she wears a carefully maintained work jacket over her pressure layers and writes times beside every observation. Sela is not eager to punish the union, but her office's power to seize the mass ledger makes her presence a constant source of pressure.","home_location_id":"loc_bastion_hulk","faction_id":"fac_charter_audit","motivation":"Make the audit findings defensible enough that neither the owners nor the union can dismiss them as factional claims.","goal":"Determine whether a hull recorded as scrapped remains in service and whether the mass ledger accounts for its power and berth.","flaw":"She avoids acting on evidence that has not passed formal verification, even when waiting gives someone time to alter the record.","internal_conflict":"Sela wants to be impartial, but fears that relying on unofficial crew testimony will make her look compromised and cost her credibility.","external_conflict":"Her audit deadline is near, the hull's thermal signature is concealed by Shadow Dock, and the owners' records may not reveal a live power connection.","arc":"Sela begins treating Nera's warning as an unverified lead and confines her inquiry to the submitted ledger. When Nera and Ivo produce matching readings and a witnessed power test before the audit is closed, Sela must choose between preserving the appearance of procedural neatness and recording what the evidence shows. She enters the discrepancy in her findings and ends more willing to verify credible crew reports before the official record can erase them.","personality_traits":["precise","reserved","skeptical","fair-minded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger examination","description":"Can compare mass entries and audit records to identify missing or inconsistent accounting.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Evidence control","description":"Can document readings and chain of custody so findings withstand challenge.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_dax_orrin","name":"Dax Orrin","role":"antagonist","description":"Dax is a Helio Tank Consortium operations representative based at the Bastion Hulk, responsible for keeping the yard productive and its charter intact. He came up through the owners' logistics offices and sees a reserve hull as insurance against fleet delays, not as a moral question. Tall and meticulously groomed, he keeps his sleeves sealed against the grit of the work decks and speaks in calm forecasts even when a crew is angry. He arranged for the scrapped hull to draw power while it waited in Shadow Dock and wants to keep that arrangement out of the audit.","home_location_id":"loc_bastion_hulk","faction_id":"fac_helio_tank","motivation":"Preserve the yard's operating capacity and the consortium's control over its salvage assets.","goal":"Prevent the audit from establishing that the hidden hull is active and force the yard to accept longer sunside shifts to meet the consortium's schedule.","flaw":"He reduces people and safety limits to entries in a production model, assuming any cost can be managed if it is not recorded.","internal_conflict":"Dax tells himself that keeping an unlisted reserve hull protects the yard from shortages, but he knows that concealment makes the union's safety and mass rules meaningless.","external_conflict":"Nera's power readings, Ivo's roster records, and Sela's audit authority threaten to expose the unlogged hull and the consortium's effort to extend heat-roster limits.","arc":"Dax begins convinced that the hidden reserve and longer shifts are practical compromises that no one needs to know about. When Nera's witnessed power test makes the live hull impossible to dismiss, he must choose whether to destroy the remaining confidence in the ledger by denying what the records show. He instead identifies the hull as an intentional reserve in his audit statement, ending with a public admission of the concealment but still facing the consequences of having treated safety limits as negotiable.","personality_traits":["calculating","composed","pragmatic","controlling"],"abilities":[{"name":"Operational planning","description":"Can allocate yard resources and estimate the production effects of competing schedules.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Institutional persuasion","description":"Can frame operational decisions in terms likely to appeal to consortium leadership.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nera_ivo","source_character_id":"chr_nera_voss","target_character_id":"chr_ivo_renn","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Nera Voss depends on Ivo Renn's access to union rosters to corroborate her hull readings, while Ivo's demand for careful procedure frustrates her urgency."},{"id":"rel_ivo_dax","source_character_id":"chr_ivo_renn","target_character_id":"chr_dax_orrin","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Ivo Renn opposes Dax Orrin's push for longer sunside shifts, seeing it as a direct threat to the charter that the union is tasked with enforcing."},{"id":"rel_nera_sela","source_character_id":"chr_nera_voss","target_character_id":"chr_sela_morin","relationship_type":"uneasy_ally","description":"Nera Voss needs Sela Morin to make the live power draw count as audit evidence, while Sela's insistence on verification makes Nera fear the deadline will pass."},{"id":"rel_sela_dax","source_character_id":"chr_sela_morin","target_character_id":"chr_dax_orrin","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Sela Morin's audit authority threatens Dax Orrin's effort to keep the reserve hull and its power draw off the mass ledger."}]}
