gory":"mental"},{"name":"Caravan accounting","description":"Keeps careful hand tallies of sealed measures and can spot inconsistencies across records.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_olen_barr","name":"Olen Barr","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_ford_market","faction_id":"fac_millers_compact","description":"Olen is a miller and ledger keeper at Ford Market, raised among the Compact's scales, charter marks, and river mud. His grandfather spoke bitterly of the falsified tithe ledger that split the routes, and Olen has spent years trying to prove that the market can still be trusted. Broad-shouldered and prematurely silver-haired, he wears a flour-dusted apron and carries a wooden tally board scarred by years of use.","motivation":"He wants Ford Market to be seen as an honest crossing rather than the source of every broken promise.","goal":"Find where the cut grain entered the tithe measures and protect the market charter without blaming the keepers on hearsay.","flaw":"He clings to official records even when their custody is part of the dispute.","internal_conflict":"Olen fears that questioning the ledger will make him seem disloyal to the Compact and reopen the shame of the Millers' Split.","external_conflict":"The forged tithe has put the Compact under accusation, and the keepers' caravan cannot accept the market's figures without risking its own standing.","arc":"Olen starts by insisting that the weigh-house ledger must settle the dispute. When Mara's caravan tally contradicts it, he chooses to bring the ledger and its corrections into a joint examination instead of quietly defending the charter. By admitting that records can be wrong even when their keeper is sincere, he begins repairing the trust the Millers' Split destroyed.","personality_traits":["proud","methodical","duty-bound","wry"],"abilities":[{"name":"Weigh-house measures","description":"Uses hand scales and familiar weights to measure grain and identify discrepancies.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Ledger reading","description":"Understands the market's hand-kept tithe records and can compare entries across seasons.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_sella_orn","name":"Sella Orn","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_ash_orchards","faction_id":"fac_orchard_families","description":"Sella is an orchard tender whose family took the blight-ash rows when few believed anything would grow there again. She has nursed young trees through lean seasons and remembers each graft promised from the vaults. Short and wiry, with ash-dark curls and hands roughened by pruning, she carries a bone-handled grafting knife and a strip of cloth marked with her family's planting rows.","motivation":"She wants her family and neighbors to receive the grafting stock owed to them, so their hard-won orchards can survive another winter.","goal":"Secure a witnessed count of the stock allocated to the Orchard Families before the caravan leaves the valley.","flaw":"Years of being overlooked have made her quick to assume that any compromise is another theft.","internal_conflict":"Sella wants the seedway restored but fears that trusting the keepers will cost her family what they have waited years to receive.","external_conflict":"The caravan's grain allocation appears to include stock the orchard families believe was promised to them, while the last frost makes delay dangerous.","arc":"Sella begins ready to block the caravan until the families' claim is met. When she discovers that a rushed stand at the road would leave the allocation uncounted and the young trees without a clear future, she chooses to join Mara and Olen in a witnessed inventory. She still demands what was promised, but ends able to negotiate through evidence rather than treating every shared measure as surrender.","personality_traits":["tenacious","practical","protective","impatient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grafting","description":"Selects and joins viable scions by hand, preserving scarce fruit-tree stock.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Orchard memory","description":"Remembers planting rows, promised grafts, and which families tended each blight-ash plot.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_davin_rell","name":"Davin Rell","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_ford_market","faction_id":"fac_millers_compact","description":"Davin is a junior weigh-house clerk at Ford Market who learned his trade copying figures under senior millers. After seasons of seeing the Compact's shortages blamed on the keepers, he began altering entries and mixing chaff into a portion of the tithe grain, hoping to force the caravan order to accept a lower return. Thin, restless, and ink-stained at the fingertips, he keeps his sleeves buttoned and his private tally slips folded inside his boot.","motivation":"He wants the Compact to stop bearing the cost of a tithe system he believes favors Granary Hill.","goal":"Keep the altered ledger undiscovered long enough to make the Compact's reduced grain share seem official.","flaw":"He mistakes a grievance he considers just for permission to deceive everyone affected by it.","internal_conflict":"Davin knows that the grain-truth rule condemns deliberate adulteration, yet fears that confessing will leave his community's complaint unheard and mark him as a traitor.","external_conflict":"His tampering has inflamed the conflict between the Millers' Compact and the Seed Keepers and threatens to derail the caravan before the Frost Gate closes.","arc":"Davin starts convinced that falsifying the tithe is the only way to make the Compact's losses visible. When Olen agrees to a joint inspection and the altered measures can no longer be explained away, Davin must choose between letting blame fall on the keepers or revealing his own hand. He confesses and identifies the entries he changed, accepting the consequences; his grievance remains, but he begins pursuing redress without making others pay for his deception.","personality_traits":["resentful","clever","anxious","defensive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger copying","description":"Copies market records neatly and knows how to make entries resemble the weigh-house hand.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Grain handling","description":"Works quickly with hand measures, sacks, and chaff at the weigh-house.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_olen","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_olen_barr","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Mara Vell and Olen Barr must compare the caravan's sealed measures with the Ford Market ledger; each suspects the other's institution may be hiding the source of the cut grain."},{"id":"rel_mara_sella","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_sella_orn","relationship_type":"disputed ally","description":"Mara Vell needs Sella Orn's account of the orchard claims, while Sella challenges Mara to prove that the caravan is not carrying stock owed to her families."},{"id":"rel_olen_davin","source_character_id":"chr_olen_barr","target_character_id":"chr_davin_rell","relationship_type":"supervisor","description":"Olen Barr trained Davin Rell in the weigh-house records and trusts him with their custody; Davin's tampering turns that trust into a direct conflict."},{"id":"rel_davin_mara","source_character_id":"chr_davin_rell","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Davin Rell's altered tithe entries make Mara Vell's caravan appear responsible for the diluted grain, placing her reputation and the seed stock at risk."},{"id":"rel_sella_davin","source_character_id":"chr_sella_orn","target_character_id":"chr_davin_rell","relationship_type":"accuser","description":"Sella Orn suspects Davin Rell's ledger changes have obscured the orchard families' promised grafting stock, while Davin fears her scrutiny will expose his deception."}]}
