{"world_id":"wld_underworld_ledger","characters":[{"id":"chr_neris_vell","name":"Neris Vell","role":"protagonist","description":"A junior clerk of the Order of Scribes, Neris found the miscast tally while copying arrivals into the ledgers of the Counting Halls. She grew up believing that careful work could make an impersonal system fair, and fears that the mistake may be traced to a hurried entry she once vouched for. She is narrow-shouldered, ink-stained at the cuffs, and wears her hair pinned with a sharpened quill she never uses as a weapon.","home_location_id":"loc_counting_halls","faction_id":"fac_scribes_order","motivation":"Keep a soul from being condemned by an account that does not belong to it.","goal":"Secure the scribe, weigher, and lamplighter keys for a correction before the soul reaches the Hall of Scales.","flaw":"She treats uncertainty as a personal failure and initially conceals evidence that could expose her own careless verification.","internal_conflict":"Neris must decide whether being a trustworthy scribe means protecting her reputation or admitting when her work may have contributed to an error.","external_conflict":"The Order of Scribes and the Collegium of Weighers blame each other's desks for the rising miscasts, while the sealed archive cannot be opened without a weigher's warrant.","arc":"Neris begins by quietly trying to repair the ledger without implicating herself. When Oren demands proof before issuing a warrant, she admits that her earlier verification was rushed and presents the original tally-slip rather than hide it. By the end, she accepts responsibility openly and earns the scribe's key through a correction that can withstand scrutiny.","personality_traits":["observant","wry","self-conscious","persistent"],"abilities":[{"name":"Column memory","description":"Remembers the layout and wording of ledger entries she has copied, helping her spot when a tally has landed in the wrong column.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Exact transcription","description":"Can reproduce a tally-slip and its annotations precisely, making discrepancies easier to demonstrate.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_oren_dask","name":"Oren Dask","role":"supporting","description":"A senior officer of the Collegium of Weighers, Oren certifies balances in the Hall of Scales and has spent years insisting that a consistent procedure is kinder than a sympathetic exception. He remembers the stories of the War of the Wrong Column, when rival weigher houses sent souls to be weighed twice, and guards against repeating that disorder by demanding a warrant for every archive request. He is tall and spare, with a polished scale-weight on a chain at his belt and a voice as level as a ruled line.","home_location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","faction_id":"fac_weighers","motivation":"Prevent a correction from reopening the kind of jurisdictional chaos that once darkened the Erasure Wells.","goal":"Verify the disputed account and issue a warrant for the sealed ledger only when the tally-slip supports it.","flaw":"He mistakes procedural caution for neutrality and is slow to recognize that delay can itself decide a soul's fate.","internal_conflict":"Oren believes the rules prevent arbitrary judgment, yet he knows that applying them mechanically can preserve an obvious wrong.","external_conflict":"He faces pressure from his colleagues to defend the weighers against blame and must decide whether to authorize the archive access the Lamplighter Kin require.","arc":"Oren begins by refusing Neris a warrant until she can establish a verifiable discrepancy. When she admits her own rushed verification and lays out the original tally-slip, he chooses to certify the evidence and provide the weigher's key despite the likely criticism from his Collegium. He ends still committed to procedure, but willing to use it to expose an error rather than shield his office.","personality_traits":["methodical","dry","cautious","principled"],"abilities":[{"name":"Balance certification","description":"Can examine a soul's assigned account and certify whether the recorded balance matches the formal weighing procedure.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Institutional authority","description":"Can issue a weigher's warrant for access to sealed ledgers when the evidence justifies an audit.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_sella_morn","name":"Sella Morn","role":"supporting","description":"A keeper of the Lamplighter Kin, Sella tends the sealed stacks in the Lamp Archive and knows how the old ledgers are arranged by their faint, painstaking marks. She inherited the post from a parent who taught her that a sealed page is not hers to make public; the Lamp Seal and the oath attached to it are both protection and burden. She is compact and silver-haired, with soot-dark fingertips and a hood that smells faintly of lamp oil.","home_location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","faction_id":"fac_lamplighters","motivation":"Preserve the archive and the oath that keeps its records from becoming tools of office rivalries.","goal":"Confirm which sealed ledger contains the soul's true account without reading a sealed page aloud.","flaw":"She equates silence with loyalty and has learned to let institutional caution excuse avoidable harm.","internal_conflict":"Sella must protect the archive's oath without using it as a reason to abandon a soul to a known miscast.","external_conflict":"Her Kin refuse to open sealed ledgers without a weigher's warrant, and reading a sealed page aloud would cost her lamp and post.","arc":"Sella begins by denying Neris access, determined not to risk the oath for another office's dispute. After Oren's warrant arrives, she uses the archive's indexing marks to locate the relevant ledger and validates its entry without speaking the sealed words. She gives the lamplighter's key, ending with her oath intact but no longer mistaking silence for the only form of fidelity.","personality_traits":["patient","guarded","precise","quietly compassionate"],"abilities":[{"name":"Archive navigation","description":"Reads the Lamp Archive's indexing marks and can locate a ledger without exposing its sealed page aloud.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Lamp keeping","description":"Maintains the archive lamps and recognizes when their light reveals signs of disturbed or misfiled records.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_tovan_rell","name":"Tovan Rell","role":"supporting","description":"A newly arrived mortal soul waiting at the Gate of Receipts, Tovan surrendered his tally-slip and discovered that his life had been entered under a stranger's account. In life he kept careful household books for a small ferry business, a habit that makes the mismatch on his slip unmistakable to him even if he has no authority to correct it. He appears as he did at death: broad-handed, travel-worn, and still holding the folded receipt he was told to keep.","home_location_id":"loc_gate_of_receipts","motivation":"Have his own life weighed against his own account, not another person's record.","goal":"Get the tally-slip and its discrepancy to Neris before he is called to the Hall of Scales.","flaw":"He expects every authority to dismiss him, so he withholds useful details until he is certain someone is listening.","internal_conflict":"Tovan fears that speaking up will make him seem troublesome, but staying quiet could leave the wrong account to define him.","external_conflict":"The arrival queue moves toward the Hall of Scales, where a soul weighed against a miscast ledger is sent to the Erasure Wells.","arc":"Tovan begins resigned to waiting and assumes the clerks will correct nothing for a soul with no standing. When Neris returns to the Gate of Receipts to compare his slip with the disputed entry, he points out a small notation from his own bookkeeping that distinguishes his account from the other one. He ends still dead and bound for the courts, but having chosen to make his record legible rather than surrender it to the queue.","personality_traits":["practical","wary","observant","understated"],"abilities":[{"name":"Bookkeeping eye","description":"Notices inconsistencies in dates, totals, and identifying marks from years of keeping ferry accounts.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Steady testimony","description":"Once persuaded that someone is listening, can give a clear chronological account of a transaction or record.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_neris_oren","source_character_id":"chr_neris_vell","target_character_id":"chr_oren_dask","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Neris needs Oren's warrant and weigher's key, while Oren's insistence on proof frustrates her urgent effort to keep Tovan from a wrongful weighing."},{"id":"rel_oren_neris","source_character_id":"chr_oren_dask","target_character_id":"chr_neris_vell","relationship_type":"skeptical ally","description":"Oren initially distrusts Neris's account of the miscast, but her admission of her own rushed verification persuades him to help her audit it."},{"id":"rel_neris_sella","source_character_id":"chr_neris_vell","target_character_id":"chr_sella_morn","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Neris asks Sella to locate the sealed ledger; Sella's oath-bound caution forces Neris to secure the proper warrant instead of demanding an exception."},{"id":"rel_sella_oren","source_character_id":"chr_sella_morn","target_character_id":"chr_oren_dask","relationship_type":"uneasy allies","description":"Sella will not open the sealed stacks without Oren's warrant, while Oren needs her archive knowledge to verify the account."},{"id":"rel_tovan_neris","source_character_id":"chr_tovan_rell","target_character_id":"chr_neris_vell","relationship_type":"wary ally","description":"Tovan trusts Neris with his tally-slip only after she returns to the Gate of Receipts and listens to his account of the mismatch."},{"id":"rel_neris_tovan","source_character_id":"chr_neris_vell","target_character_id":"chr_tovan_rell","relationship_type":"advocate",