own work. He ends prepared to help investigate openly, having accepted that protecting the city matters more than protecting the Collegium's image.","personality_traits":["craft-proud","measured","protective","evasive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Bell casting","description":"Can judge a casting's likely sound from its metal, shape, and visible imperfections.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Foundry authority","description":"Can identify the work practices and marks associated with the Founder Collegium's members.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_maraud_kell","name":"Maraud Kell","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_bailiffs_stairs","faction_id":"fac_parish_watch","description":"Maraud Kell is a senior warden of the Parish Watch, charged with enforcing the silence laws and delivering writs that can still a bell. He was raised in the aftermath of the Lost Parish, and his family taught him that a rule enforced too late is no protection at all. He is narrow-faced and neatly dressed in a dark watch coat, with a waxed ledger tucked inside it and a name-token worn on a cord beneath his collar. He speaks sparingly in fog and prefers written orders, believing that procedure can keep panic from becoming another disaster.","motivation":"Prevent the Chiming from taking more citizens by ensuring the parish's laws are obeyed before the fog arrives.","goal":"Have the storm-bells silenced under writ until the Parish Watch can determine whether their strange pattern endangers the city.","flaw":"He mistakes control for safety and treats uncertain evidence as a reason to impose the harshest available measure.","internal_conflict":"Maraud wants to protect the people whose names the salt registry preserves, but doubts that the rules he enforces can protect them when the bells themselves become suspect.","external_conflict":"Elin and the founders insist the bells must be investigated, while Maraud is responsible for carrying out the parish order before the next fog.","arc":"Maraud begins convinced that silencing the bells is the only defensible response to an unexplained note. When Elin presents her observations at Bailiff's Stairs and Osric admits the repair records are incomplete, Maraud must choose between immediate enforcement and a witnessed inspection at the Sea-Wall Belfry. He allows the inspection under watch, ending willing to distinguish caution from reflexive suppression, though he remains responsible for enforcing the silence laws.","personality_traits":["disciplined","cautious","unyielding","dutiful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Writ enforcement","description":"Can carry out parish orders to restrict access and still a bell under the silence laws.","category":"social"},{"name":"Fog protocol","description":"Knows the watch's procedures for limiting spoken names and keeping order when fog closes in.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_vesper_dain","name":"Vesper Dain","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_fogmarket","faction_id":"fac_fog_brokers","description":"Vesper Dain is a licensed Fog Broker who trades in names and secrets at the Fogmarket under the Brokers' Charter. They were once a clerk at the Salt Chapel, where they learned how much a registry can preserve and how easily its omissions can become a person's undoing. Vesper is tall and fine-boned, dressed in a hooded oilcloth coat with a chain of blank name-tokens at the wrist. They keep their own name unspoken in fog and make every bargain precise, even when the cost to someone else is not.","motivation":"Keep the chartered market—and the leverage it gives its brokers—out of the Parish Watch's control.","goal":"Find out who is trading in the unmarked bell's secret and ensure the Fog Brokers are not blamed for the strange ringing.","flaw":"They reduce trust to a transaction and assume every useful truth must be bought or withheld.","internal_conflict":"Vesper values the security the charter provides, but knows that trading in names can leave citizens as exposed as the fog itself.","external_conflict":"The watch's scrutiny of name-debts threatens the Fogmarket's charter, while the bell pattern could provoke another attempt to control what citizens are allowed to know.","arc":"Vesper begins intent on keeping the bell mystery within the market as a bargaining secret. When Maraud's writ threatens to close off access to the Sea-Wall Belfry and the Fogmarket's own charter becomes a target, Vesper chooses to give Elin a lead from the market without demanding a name in payment. They end still a broker, but willing to risk a profitable secret when keeping it hidden would strengthen the watch's grip.","personality_traits":["shrewd","composed","transactional","attentive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Market negotiation","description":"Can navigate the Fogmarket's chartered bargains and recognize when a supposed secret is being used as leverage.","category":"social"},{"name":"Registry knowledge","description":"Understands how the Salt Chapel's name records are kept and what it means for a name to be unregistered.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_elin_osric","source_character_id":"chr_elin_voss","target_character_id":"chr_osric_tane","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Elin Voss is Osric Tane's apprentice; she trusts his craft knowledge but resents his demand for silence when the pattern contradicts the Collegium's claims."},{"id":"rel_osric_elin","source_character_id":"chr_osric_tane","target_character_id":"chr_elin_voss","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Osric Tane sees Elin Voss as a promising founder whose candor could expose the Collegium, creating a conflict between his care for her and his instinct to protect the institution."},{"id":"rel_elin_maraud","source_character_id":"chr_elin_voss","target_character_id":"chr_maraud_kell","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Elin Voss needs time to investigate the strange note, while Maraud Kell intends to enforce the writ that would silence the bells."},{"id