"motivation":"Make sure every promise and ruling is clear enough to be kept.","goal":"Determine which outstanding favours must be settled before closing day and rule fairly on Maeve's family's claim.","flaw":"She trusts written records more readily than people's accounts of what those records mean to them.","internal_conflict":"Tamsin values impartial procedure but worries that strict bookkeeping can preserve an old mistake instead of resolving it.","external_conflict":"The fair has more favours owed than can be kept before closing day, and Tamsin must judge the Ninth Claim while deciding which debts ride with the fair.","arc":"Tamsin begins by relying on the wishing tags as the complete account of every debt. When Maeve and Ives bring forward the history behind the Ninth Stall's forfeited favour, Tamsin chooses to hear both accounts before entering a ruling. She ends the season still committed to careful records, but more attentive to the people and promises they represent."},{"id":"chr_sella_mint","name":"Sella Mint","role":"supporting","description":"A tea merchant and member of the Stallholders' Round who runs a bright tent in the Kettle Commons. Sella is known for blending fragrant teas from ingredients traded around the fair, and for remembering which merchant prefers a quiet cup over a public speech. She wears a copper-colored shawl over a flour-dusted dress and decorates her tent with jars of dried leaves. Having watched many stallholders overextend themselves, she values sustainable bargains over dramatic gestures.","home_location_id":"loc_kettle_commons","faction_id":"fac_stallholders","motivation":"Keep the Commons a welcoming place where merchants can trade without fear of unpayable promises.","goal":"Help Maeve put forward a workable tea-and-trade bargain for the Ninth Stall before the Stallholders' Round votes.","flaw":"She stays neutral for so long that people may mistake her caution for indifference.","internal_conflict":"Sella wants to protect the fair from another broken promise, but fears that taking sides will make the Round's decision less fair.","external_conflict":"The Stallholders' Round must consider the disputed Ninth Stall lease while the shortage of favours makes every proposed bargain consequential.","arc":"Sella begins by offering Maeve tea and advice but avoids speaking publicly about the disputed lease. When the Round's vote approaches and Maeve's bargain risks being overlooked, Sella chooses to present a sample-trade plan and explain why it can be kept. She ends the season more willing to use her standing in the Round when careful neutrality would leave a sound solution unheard."}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maeve_ives","source_character_id":"chr_maeve_bramble","target_character_id":"chr_ives_carrow","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Maeve opposes Ives's effort to sell the Ninth Stall lease before her family's claim is heard, but their shared respect for fair trade gives them room to negotiate."},{"id":"rel_ives_maeve","source_character_id":"chr_ives_carrow","target_character_id":"chr_maeve_bramble","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Ives sees Maeve as the person who could complicate his kin's sale, yet he gradually becomes her ally in making the lease terms honest and understandable."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_maeve","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_wick","target_character_id":"chr_maeve_bramble","relationship_type":"arbiter","description":"Tamsin must judge Maeve's family claim and the favour attached to it, pressing Maeve to distinguish a heartfelt promise from one she can actually keep."},{"id":"rel_sella_maeve","source_character_id":"chr_sella_mint","target_character_id":"chr_maeve_bramble","relationship_type":"friend","description":"Sella is Maeve's fellow tea merchant and supports her with samples and practical advice, while encouraging her not to shoulder the claim alone."},{"id":"rel_sella_ives","source_character_id":"chr_sella_mint","target_character_id":"chr_ives_carrow","relationship_type":"negotiator","description":"Sella challenges Ives to put the Carter Kin's proposed sale before the Stallholders' Round openly, helping turn his quick transaction into a bargain others can assess."}]}
