{"world_id":"wld_comet_market","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_vell","name":"Mara Vell","role":"protagonist","description":"A quick-witted factotum of the Mapmakers' Guild, Mara grew up tallying ice-tithes and carrying sealed charts between the Map House and the Long Hall. After her mentor was lost during the Map Wars, she learned to trust procedure more than people. She is lean, sharp-eyed, and usually wears a guild coat with ink-stained cuffs and a ring of brass keys.","motivation":"Keep the market's arbitration credible when the stolen perihelion map threatens to turn old grudges into open flight.","goal":"Determine who stole and resold the sealed star-map before the burn articles force the fleet to settle or forfeit its claims.","flaw":"She clings to procedure even when it shields the powerful or leaves the vulnerable stranded.","internal_conflict":"Mara fears that acting on compassion rather than evidence will make her indistinguishable from the guild officials who once concealed her mentor's mistakes.","external_conflict":"As acting arbiter, she must resolve the map dispute under a rule that permits opening the seal only by its sealer or the Long Hall arbiter, while pilots and mapmakers contest her authority.","arc":"Mara begins convinced that a strictly formal hearing is the only way to preserve order. When the Ice Barons move to claim unpaid pilots' tethers before the burn, she chooses to hear the pilot's salvage evidence in public rather than let guild procedure bury it. She ends willing to use her authority transparently and accept personal blame for a just ruling.","home_location_id":"loc_long_hall","faction_id":"fac_mapmakers","personality_traits":["observant","dry-humored","methodical","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Claim ledger","description":"Can trace berth payments, map registrations, and ownership transfers through the guild's records.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Hearing craft","description":"Questions witnesses carefully and spots contradictions without confusing suspicion for proof.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ren_tallis","name":"Ren Tallis","role":"supporting","description":"A Free Pilots' Compact navigator, Ren holds the disputed chart after buying it from a desperate intermediary and claims it was salvage from a ship that had already abandoned its route. Raised among tether crews, Ren learned to judge a vessel by its rigging and a promise by whether it survives a hard burn. They are broad-shouldered, sun-browned, and wear a patched flight harness with a harpoon line coiled at the hip.","motivation":"Protect independent pilots from being treated as trespassers on routes they have flown for generations.","goal":"Prove the chart was abandoned salvage and keep the Ice Barons from using the dispute to take indebted pilots' tether rights.","flaw":"Ren's pride makes them conceal bad bargains until those bargains endanger everyone around them.","internal_conflict":"They want the Compact to trust their judgment but fear that admitting how little they know about the chart's chain of custody will make them look like a guild pawn.","external_conflict":"The Mapmakers call Ren a thief, while the sealed chart's unknown seller and the approaching perihelion leave little time to establish its provenance.","arc":"Ren starts by insisting that buying the chart makes the matter simple. When Mara's hearing reveals that the sale may have been arranged to trigger forfeitures under the burn articles, Ren chooses to disclose the seller's identity despite risking the Compact's confidence. They end with a weaker claim to the map but a stronger place in the pilots' cause.","home_location_id":"loc_tether_docks","faction_id":"fac_free_pilots","personality_traits":["bold","resourceful","proud","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tether handling","description":"Can secure and maneuver a ship against the comet's slow spin using lines, sails, and reaction plumes.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Route memory","description":"Remembers practical hazards and drift patterns along routes flown by the Compact.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_ilesa_quill","name":"Ilesa Quill","role":"antagonist","description":"The Mapmakers' senior sealer, Ilesa has guarded the guild's route records since the last years of the Map Wars. She believes public confidence in sealed charts is the only thing keeping rival pilots from steering the fleet into catastrophe. Immaculately dressed in dark blue, she carries a seal case chained to her wrist and speaks with the calm precision of a clerk reading a sentence.","motivation":"Preserve the guild's control over route certification so no unverified chart can endanger the fleet.","goal":"Recover the stolen map, identify who broke its custody, and prevent the hearing from legitimizing Ren's salvage claim.","flaw":"She treats institutional authority as proof of moral authority.","internal_conflict":"Ilesa knows that a map's seal is meant to prevent dangerous tampering, yet fears that admitting the guild can fail will reopen the rivalries that nearly wrecked the fleet.","external_conflict":"Mara's hearing threatens to expose gaps in the map's custody, while Ilesa's own sealing authority makes her both a vital witness and a suspect in the dispute.","arc":"Ilesa begins certain that restoring the chart to the guild is enough to end the crisis. When Mara asks her to account publicly for a gap in the seal register, Ilesa must choose between concealing it and letting the Ice Barons exploit the uncertainty. She admits the register's failure, sacrificing her spotless reputation to help establish the truth and preserve the guild's legitimacy on honest terms.","home_location_id":"loc_map_house","faction_id":"fac_mapmakers","personality_traits":["composed","exacting","proud","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Seal verification","description":"Recognizes the guild's sealing marks and can identify signs of tampering without opening a chart.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Guild negotiation","description":"Knows how to secure testimony and concessions from guild officers without making a dispute public prematurely.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_daro_senn","name":"Daro Senn","role":"supporting","description":"An Ice Barons' claims broker, Daro negotiates core rights and buys tether claims ahead of each burn. He grew up in the Core Vaults and believes that orderly ownership is the only defense against a market where every orbit can erase a fortune. His silver-threaded gloves and immaculate boots contrast with the frost-scored coat he refuses to replace.","motivation":"Secure enough tether rights to keep the Barons' core claims productive through the coming burn.","goal":"Use the map dispute and unpaid ice-tithes to purchase or claim berths before the fleet scatters.","flaw":"He mistakes a legal advantage for a fair outcome and rarely considers who pays its human cost.","internal_conflict":"Daro wants to be seen as a guardian of the market's stability, but his business depends on the very fear and debt that make pilots vulnerable.","external_conflict":"The Compact opposes the Barons' tether purchases, and Mara's arbitration could invalidate the leverage Daro has assembled before perihelion.","arc":"Daro begins treating the hearing as an opportunity to strengthen the Barons' claims. When Ren's evidence shows that the chart sale was used to push debtors toward forfeiture, Daro is offered a chance to deny involvement or reveal the broker who arranged it. He names the broker, accepting a costly setback and ending as a more credible negotiator rather than an opportunist hiding behind the articles.","home_location_id":"loc_core_vaults","faction_id":"fac_ice_barons","personality_traits":["calculating","patient","formal","pragmatic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Claims accounting","description":"Calculates the value and deadlines of ice claims, tithes, and tether rights.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Bargaining","description":"Can negotiate complex exchanges while keeping track of what each side risks before the burn.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_sela_orren","name":"Sela Orren","role":"supporting","description":"A grower in the Cinder Gardens, Sela tends glasshouse crops that rely on the comet's perihelion light and supplies provisions to crews preparing for the burn. She once piloted for the Compact but left after a reckless run cost her sibling a berth. Sela is wiry, silver-haired, and keeps a gardener's knife tucked into a stained apron.","motivation":"Make sure the market's ordinary crews survive the burn, not just the claim-holders who can afford to scatter early.","goal":"Get the hearing to account for the pilots and garden hands who will lose food, berths, or safe passage if the map dispute delays preparations.","flaw":"She keeps painful information to herself until she is certain no one can misuse it.","internal_conflict":"Sela wants to help the Compact but fears that choosing a side will repeat the divided loyalties that drove her from piloting.","external_conflict":"The hearing's focus on the map and tether claims threatens to overlook the Cinder Gardens' supplies and the crews whose survival depends on timely decisions.","arc":"Sela begins as a wary bystander who offers only provisions. When Mara's hearing risks closing before the garden crews' evidence is heard, Sela chooses to testify about the timing of supplies and the broker's visits, despite exposing her old ties to the Compact. She ends committed to speaking before silence makes the vulnerable easy to bargain away.","home_location_id":"loc_cinder_gardens","personality_traits":["practical","cautious","compassionate","self-reliant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Perihelion growing","description":"Knows how to time crops and preserve provisions through the comet's changing light and heat.","category":"other"},{"name":"Crew reading","description":"Recognizes when exhausted crews are being pressured into bad bargains or unsafe departures.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_ren","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_ren_tallis","relationship_type":"arbiter and claimant","description":"Mara must judge Ren's salvage claim; Ren's guarded testimony tests whether Mara can distinguish due process from guild loyalty."},{"id":"rel_ilesa_mara","source_character_id":"chr_ilesa_quill","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"mentor and challenger","description":"Ilesa trained Mara in guild procedure and now pressures her to restore the map without exposing the guild's custody failures."},{"id":"rel_daro_ren","source_character_id":"chr_daro_senn","target_character_id":"chr_ren_tallis","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Daro's purchases of indebted pilots' tether rights threaten Ren's Compact, while Ren's claim could undermine the Barons' leverage."},{"id":"rel_sela_ren","source_character_id":"chr_sela_orren","target_character_id":"chr_ren_tallis","relationship_type":"former comrades","description":"Sela and Ren once flew together; Sela's departure after her sibling lost a berth makes her wary of Ren's appetite for risk."},{"id":"rel_mara_ilesa","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_ilesa_quill","relationship_type":"rivals","description":"Mara respects Ilesa's expertise but challenges her assumption that the guild's authority should shield its own records from scrutiny."}]}
