otiation","description":"Knows how to secure testimony and concessions from guild officers without making a dispute public prematurely.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_daro_senn","name":"Daro Senn","role":"supporting","description":"An Ice Barons' claims broker, Daro negotiates core rights and buys tether claims ahead of each burn. He grew up in the Core Vaults and believes that orderly ownership is the only defense against a market where every orbit can erase a fortune. His silver-threaded gloves and immaculate boots contrast with the frost-scored coat he refuses to replace.","motivation":"Secure enough tether rights to keep the Barons' core claims productive through the coming burn.","goal":"Use the map dispute and unpaid ice-tithes to purchase or claim berths before the fleet scatters.","flaw":"He mistakes a legal advantage for a fair outcome and rarely considers who pays its human cost.","internal_conflict":"Daro wants to be seen as a guardian of the market's stability, but his business depends on the very fear and debt that make pilots vulnerable.","external_conflict":"The Compact opposes the Barons' tether purchases, and Mara's arbitration could invalidate the leverage Daro has assembled before perihelion.","arc":"Daro begins treating the hearing as an opportunity to strengthen the Barons' claims. When Ren's evidence shows that the chart sale was used to push debtors toward forfeiture, Daro is offered a chance to deny involvement or reveal the broker who arranged it. He names the broker, accepting a costly setback and ending as a more credible negotiator rather than an opportunist hiding behind the articles.","home_location_id":"loc_core_vaults","faction_id":"fac_ice_barons","personality_traits":["calculating","patient","formal","pragmatic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Claims accounting","description":"Calculates the value and deadlines of ice claims, tithes, and tether rights.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Bargaining","description":"Can negotiate complex exchanges while keeping track of what each side risks before the burn.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_sela_orren","name":"Sela Orren","role":"supporting","description":"A grower in the Cinder Gardens, Sela tends glasshouse crops that rely on the comet's perihelion light and supplies provisions to crews preparing for the burn. She once piloted for the Compact but left after a reckless run cost her sibling a berth. Sela is wiry, silver-haired, and keeps a gardener's knife tucked into a stained apron.","motivation":"Make sure the market's ordinary crews survive the burn, not just the claim-holders who can afford to scatter early.","goal":"Get the hearing to account for the pilots and garden hands who will lose food, berths, or safe passage if the map dispute delays preparations.","flaw":"She keeps painful information to herself until she is certain no one can misuse it.","internal_conflict":"Sela wants to help the Compact but fears that choosing a side will repeat the divided loyalties that drove her from piloting.","external_conflict":"The hearing's focus on the map and tether claims threatens to overlook the Cinder Gardens' supplies and the crews whose survival depends on timely decisions.","arc":"Sela begins as a wary bystander who offers only provisions. When Mara's hearing risks closing before the garden crews' evidence is heard, Sela chooses to testify about the timing of supplies and the broker's visits, despite exposing her old ties to the Compact. She ends committed to speaking before silence makes the vulnerable easy to bargain away.","home_location_id":"loc_cinder_gardens","personality_traits":["practical","cautious","compassionate","self-reliant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Perihelion growing","description":"Knows how to time crops and preserve provisions through the comet's changing light and heat.","category":"other"},{"name":"Crew reading","description":"Recognizes when exhausted crews are being pressured into bad bargains or unsafe departures.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_ren","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_ren_tallis","relationship_type":"arbiter and claimant","description":"Mara must judge Ren's salvage claim; Ren's guarded testimony tests whether Mara can distinguish due process from guild loyalty."},{"id":"rel_ilesa_mara","source_character_id":"chr_ilesa_quill","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"mentor and challenger","description":"Ilesa trained Mara in guild procedure and now pressures her to restore the map without exposing the guild's custody failures."},{"id":"rel_daro_ren","source_character_id":"chr_daro_senn","target_character_id":"chr_ren_tallis","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Daro's purchases of indebted pilots' tether rights threaten Ren's Compact, while Ren's claim could undermine the Barons' leverage."},{"id":"rel_sela_ren","source_character_id":"chr_sela_orren","target_character_id":"chr_ren_tallis","relationship_type":"former comrades","description":"Sela and Ren once flew together; Sela's departure after her sibling lost a berth makes her wary of Ren's appetite for risk."},{"id":"rel_mara_ilesa","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_ilesa_quill","relationship_type":"rivals","description":"Mara respects Ilesa's expertise but challenges her assumption that the guild's authority should shield its own records from scrutiny."}]}
