ailing priorities.","category":"social"},{"name":"Harbour timing","description":"Understands how tides, pilots' observations, and the monsoon season constrain a fleet's departure.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_ferdinand_sorell","name":"Ferdinand Sorell","description":"Ferdinand is an envoy for a western trading delegation whose factors have tied much of their fortune to pepper waiting in the bonded warehouses. He dresses in dark, carefully mended wool suited poorly to the humid port and carries himself like a man accustomed to being heard first. His fluency in contracts is genuine, but years of political bargaining have taught him to treat every rule as an obstacle to be managed.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_envoy_house","faction_id":"fac_pepper_factors","motivation":"Avoid the commercial and political disgrace of returning with a season lost and his delegation's investment stranded.","goal":"Make the court recognize his delegation's claim as the earliest and secure the first sailing slot.","flaw":"He believes a favorable outcome excuses bending the process, especially when he can disguise pressure as customary hospitality.","internal_conflict":"Ferdinand wants to believe he is protecting his delegation, but knows that his attempts to influence the slot-keepers could make their claim look bought rather than earned.","external_conflict":"His claim is one of three filed in the same hour, and the unregistered gifts found in the pepper warehouses put his dealings under scrutiny just as the sailing window approaches.","arc":"Ferdinand begins certain that influence can repair any weakness in his claim. When Mira connects the warehouse gifts to the gift register and refuses to treat them as harmless courtesy, he must choose between denying his part and making the gifts public. He discloses what he knows, losing the advantage of secrecy but ending with a claim the court can judge on its record rather than on concealed pressure.","personality_traits":["ambitious","polished","impatient","calculating"],"abilities":[{"name":"Contract rhetoric","description":"Frames commercial claims in persuasive language and quickly identifies ambiguities in an agreement.","category":"social"},{"name":"Trade arithmetic","description":"Estimates the cost of delay and the leverage held by cargo owners waiting for the monsoon.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mira_yusuf","source_character_id":"chr_mira_vellan","target_character_id":"chr_yusuf_albari","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mira must test Yusuf's claim against the ledger despite his courtesy; Yusuf sees her as the official whose ruling may cost his fleet its season."},{"id":"rel_mira_laleh","source_character_id":"chr_mira_vellan","target_character_id":"chr_laleh_banu","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Mira and Laleh both want an accountable hearing, but Laleh distrusts the court and presses Mira to make the Majlis's evidence public."},{"id":"rel_mira_ferdinand","source_character_id":"chr_mira_vellan","target_character_id":"chr_ferdinand_sorell","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Mira investigates the unregistered gifts tied to Ferdinand's delegation, while he challenges her authority to question the means by which his claim was supported."},{"id":"rel_yusuf_laleh","source_character_id":"chr_yusuf_albari","target_character_id":"chr_laleh_banu","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Yusuf and Laleh compete for the first slot, but both know that a prolonged deadlock could cost their fleets the monsoon season."},{"id":"rel_ferdinand_yusuf","source_character_id":"chr_ferdinand_sorell","target_character_id":"chr_yusuf_albari","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Ferdinand treats Yusuf's careful documentation as a threat to his own claim and tries to make the court doubt Yusuf's account."}]}
