sing document and dismisses Mara's observations as insufficient evidence. When she sees that the ledger's silence has allowed the factions to shift the oil burden onto the turf-cutters, she chooses to record their testimony alongside the surviving entries. She ends committed to a ledger that acknowledges uncertainty instead of disguising it as certainty.","personality_traits":["methodical","skeptical","conscientious","reserved"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger hand","description":"Can compare entries, identify altered or missing sequences, and preserve an accurate account in difficult conditions.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Council mediation","description":"Knows how to frame a dispute so rival parish members will hear one another before the moot breaks apart.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tomas_bell","name":"Tomas Bell","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_bog_hollow","faction_id":"fac_turf_cutters","description":"Tomas Bell is a turf-cutter whose family has worked the Bog Hollow for generations and owes oil to the wall. He is broad-shouldered, with peat-stained hands, a stiff knee, and a strip of pale scar along one cheek from a cutting tool. He knows the bog's paths by daylight and the ways sound travels over wet ground, but refuses to carry a lantern past the bog line after dusk. Years of disputed tithe counts have made him wary of any warden who arrives with a tally already written.","motivation":"To keep his family from being driven into debt by an oil tithe he believes the wardens have over-counted.","goal":"Make the council verify the turf-cutters' contribution and ensure the wall has enough oil without taking more than the families owe.","flaw":"His resentment makes him assume every request from the wardens is another attempt to shift the burden onto his family.","internal_conflict":"Tomas wants to protect his own household first, but knows that if the wall fails, no family in the parish can remain safe.","external_conflict":"The shortfall places the wall at risk, the wardens accuse the cutters of withholding oil, and the bog's darkness limits what Tomas is willing to investigate after dusk.","arc":"Tomas begins refusing to help until the wardens admit their tithe count is wrong. When Mara's watch shows that every measure matters and Elspeth offers to record the cutters' account, he chooses to bring his family's oil tally to the Moot Kirk rather than let the dispute starve the wall. He ends prepared to contribute what is truly owed while openly challenging any count that would make his family pay for another faction's silence.","personality_traits":["resourceful","wary","plainspoken","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Moorcraft","description":"Reads the bog's safe ground and recognizes changes in peat, water, and sound without needing a lantern after dusk.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Fair measure","description":"Keeps careful household tallies and can spot when a claimed oil contribution does not match the amount supplied.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_owen","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vane","target_character_id":"chr_owen_rusk","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Vane's insistence on an honest account pits her against Owen Rusk, whose secrecy she sees as a threat to the wall's watch."},{"id":"rel_owen_mara","source_character_id":"chr_owen_rusk","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vane","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Owen Rusk trained Mara Vane in the wall watch, but his guarded lessons and refusal to discuss the missing page turn his mentorship into a contest over trust."},{"id":"rel_mara_elspeth","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vane","target_character_id":"chr_elspeth_cairn","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara Vane brings Elspeth Cairn observations from the wall, and Elspeth helps her test those observations against the surviving ledger."},{"id":"rel_elspeth_owen","source_character_id":"chr_elspeth_cairn","target_character_id":"chr_owen_rusk","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Elspeth Cairn demands that Owen Rusk account for the missing ledger page, while he fears her record will expose the wardens' part in its disappearance."},{"id":"rel_tomas_owen","source_character_id":"chr_tomas_bell","target_character_id":"chr_owen_rusk","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tomas Bell disputes Owen Rusk's oil tally and suspects the senior warden is making the turf-cutters pay for the wardens' shortfall."},{"id":"rel_tomas_mara","source_character_id":"chr_tomas_bell","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tomas Bell initially distrusts Mara Vane as a warden, but her willingness to hear the cutters' account earns his help in keeping the wall supplied."}]}
